    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1541">

                <pb facs="1675" n="1661" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.6363/1633: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-22T22:00:00-04:30">April 22, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 23—2:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>435. Terms of new concession bids cited in Department’s 259 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">359</hi>], April 22, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d1541-f1"/> have been discussed with British Minister<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d1541-f2"/> and are reported in air mail despatch leaving by today’s
                        pouch.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d1541-f3"/> They involve an attempt to assure
                    refining of 10% of Venezuelan crude in Venezuela and shipment of remaining 90%
                    out of Caribbean area in crude form. Effect would be to by-pass Aruba and
                    Curaçao. Proposal affects Shell<anchor n="46" xml:id="d1541-f4"/> interests much
                    more vitally than it does our own.</p>
                <p>Head of largest American producing company here considers this an administrative
                    proposal which can be overcome and does not think it calls for diplomatic
                    protests at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
